From be05a35d94d185e3caa125b544a9b9bcafba256e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrija Panic <andrija.panic@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 01:08:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add UEFI bootloader fix rule for Debian 11

Debian 11 uses the same shim-based EFI layout as Debian 12 but was
missing from the UEFI fix pattern match, causing converted UEFI VMs
to fail to boot with "No UEFI fix rule for debian 11".

Resolves: https://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/RHEL-167109

Backport to virt-v2v 2.7.1 (rhel-9.8) of upstream commit
01288ce7914e6daf6c521b16bfafae799186e0e4 by Surya Gupta
<surygupt@redhat.com>, pull request
https://github.com/libguestfs/virt-v2v/pull/195, released in
virt-v2v 2.13.7.  Applied without conflicts.

(cherry picked from commit 01288ce7914e6daf6c521b16bfafae799186e0e4)
---
 convert/convert_linux.ml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/convert/convert_linux.ml b/convert/convert_linux.ml
index e295a01d..31d249b8 100644
--- a/convert/convert_linux.ml
+++ b/convert/convert_linux.ml
@@ -1390,7 +1390,7 @@ let convert (g : G.guestfs) source inspect i_firmware _ keep_serial_console _ =
                   g inspect.i_root "fix uefi boot" fix_script)
               else
                 cant_fix_uefi ()
-            | ("ubuntu", 14) | ("debian", 12)->
+            | ("ubuntu", 14) | ("debian", 11) | ("debian", 12) ->
               (* to make a bootable uefi ubuntu 14 we need to
                * copy shim<arch>.efi to UEFI fallback path
                * and rename it to BOOT<arch>.efi, also we copy
-- 
